# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
/open-crank-mcp
*.pdx

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Simulator Data directory bind-mounted by the shared profile. Holds a running
# game's save data and mcp/game_logs.json. Root-owned, since the container
# runs as root.
/.shared-data/

# Same directory under its pre-rename name. Still ignored so an existing
# checkout doesn't show it as untracked: it's root-owned, so clearing it needs
# sudo or a container, and nobody should be forced to do that just to get a
# clean `git status`. See the README's migration note.
/.byos-data/

# Artifacts the contract tests leave in the fixtures.
#
# internal/contracttest builds lua/test-fixture and c-harness/test/fixture-game
# in place rather than in a copy, and runs `setup` against them, which vendors a
# harness into each. Inside the container that touched a copy of the repo baked
# into the image, so it was invisible. `make sdk-contract-check-native` runs in
# the real working tree, so it is not.
#
# Generated either way, and never worth committing.
/c-harness/test/fixture-game/build/
/c-harness/test/fixture-game/src/mcp_harness.c
/c-harness/test/fixture-game/src/mcp_harness.h
/lua/test-fixture/Source/mcp_harness.lua

# Editor/IDE
# .vscode/

# IntelliJ / GoLand. Covers the project directory wherever it sits, plus the
# module and workspace files those IDEs write next to it.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
out/

# Browser test dependencies and output, installed into the mounted directory by
# the Playwright container, so root-owned on the host.
/tests/browser/node_modules/
/tests/browser/test-results/
/tests/browser/playwright-report/
